          ":question/problem": "Given that\n$$\nS=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$,\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes ${a}_{33}=0?$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation \n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}={R}_{3}+(-3)\\cdot {R}_{1}\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is \n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3)\\cdot {R}_{1}\n$$\n\nor simply\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}.\n$$"
